<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/A-Step-in-the-Right-Direction.jpg" alt="A figurative painting of a young rooster with gray background" width="350" height="483" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">A Step in the Right Direction. 16" x 12" oil on linen panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I spent most of February 2014 working on landscape paintings, some of which were more successful than others. &nbsp;For a change of pace I looked through some photos I took last year and found some nice images of a rooster that I'd previously painted from a different angle. &nbsp;</p>
<p>After a month of trying to mix and paint with delicate grays I enjoyed having the opportunity to paint with full-strength colors.</p>
<p>I'm setting this painting aside for the Upperville Stable Tour and I'll try to add another rooster to the portfolio in time for that event.</p>